On 19 Dec 2005 16:09:37 -0800, dunric@yahoo.com wrote:

> I am a programmer
> myself and the idea of compressing something to 1 byte -- universally
> -- has always intrigued me.

It's insane.

There are only 256 different one-byte strings. There are far more than 256
different datasets you might want to compress.  Therefore, if it is meant
to be possible to decompress uniquely from 1 byte back to the original,
then there must be many, many different source datasets that cannot have a
1-byte string as the compressed result.


