I have a couple of 256-MB EZ disks.  I used to use them for page/swap 
files (handy if the machine has only 48 MB RAM!) but they don't work 
anymore.  A single disk works fine, and I can build a shadow set, but 
when the shadow copy is about 99% complete, the shadow set starts going 
in and out of mount verification several times a second and the only way 
out is to power-cycle the machine.

This behaviour started after an upgrade, if I recall correctly either
the upgrade to VMS 7.3-2 or after applying a SHADOWING and/or SYSTEM
and/or UPDATE patch.  Since I can live without these disks, I didn't try
rebooting from the backup system disk to check the old behaviour.
However, since the disks seem OK physically, and work as individual
disk, I suspect a VMS bug.

Is anyone using such disks with a fully patched 7.3-2 system?



