:
:   I'm trying to get a hardware maintenance contract from HP.  One of
:   my systems, an Infoserver-1000, has the following model number on
:   its tag:
:
:      70-30343-03. A02
:
:   HP claims that "703034303A" is not a valid model number.

  The 2-5-2 format is a classic DIGITAL part number.

  The serial number will begin with two characters (tied to
  a DIGITAL site code, such as WM, ZK or NI, followed by some
  number of letters and (usually mostly or all) numbers.

:   Is this a punctuation problem, or is HP looking for some other
:   number?

  The latter.

  The serial number sticker is located on the bottom of the InfoServer 
  1000 itself, and clearly labeled with the model number and with the 
  classic "SN" prefix indicating the serial number of the device.
  Pull the cables off the back, slide the release lever to the left,
  and pull the device out of the shelf for a look.)

  We now have InfoServer support built directly into current versions
  of OpenVMS, as another alternative to the older InfoServer hardware.
  You can use an AlphaServer, for instance, for InfoServer services.
  (Not including the CD recording that was once provided by the old
  and optional InfoServer Scribe package, though that capability is 
  also available within OpenVMS V7.3-1 and later.)

