Not Windows for Workgroups and later, but DOS,  with at wish Windows 3.1,
could boot from a VAX with PCSA. FRB (flopy remote boot) was the name of that
facility. Drivers for then current network cards like the DExxx and 3COM cards
were supported. One of the disk images in the vaxmate archive is the FRB floppy
for PCSA V2.2, which was DECnet. PCSA V3 brought other protocol stacks.
