David J Dachtera <djesys.nospam@comcast.net> writes:

>Schnootling wrote:
>> 
>> Hi John,
>> 
>> Can OpenVMS (Hobbyist) run on a GS140 ?

>VMS is VMS is VMS is ... (i.e., there is no "hobbyist version").

>...and yes, the GS140 runs OpenVMS.

That is true, but there is a difference in the _licenses_ that allow
VMS.  If you bought, say, an alphastation 200 with a commercial VMS
license, you couldn't just transfer everything including the license
to a GS140 and expect it to run.  The VMS license won't allow it.

Having said that, the hobbyist license is set up to allow VMS to run
on anything, so yes, a hobbyist can run VMS on a GS140.


