In article <1133812652.742141.60140@g47g2000cwa.googlegroups.com>, "Bob Armstrong" <bob@jfcl.com> writes:

:  Do the KA655 (uVAX-III+) and KA650 (uVAX-III) use the same MS650
:(M7622) memory boards, or is there actually such a thing as a MS655?
:If there is, does anybody know the Mxxxx module number for the latter?

  The MS650-BA/-BF series memory module (M7622-A*) is compatible with
  the MicroVAX III and MicroVAX III+ series, and with various of the
  VAXstation 3200, VAXstation 3500, MicroVAX 3500, and MicroVAX 3800
  systems based on the KA650 or on the the KA655-series processor 
  modules, while both the MS650-AA/-AF and MS650-BA/-BF memory modules
  are compatible with the MicroVAX III, VAXstation 3200, etc. KA650
  series systems.

  The MS650-A* series memories only work on the KA650 series processor,
  in other words, and not with the KA655 series processors.  The MS650-B*
  series memory works with both processors.

  Do ensure you have a correct and current-revision private memory 
  interconnect cable, and do NOT use the 17-02174-* nor 17-00716-* 
  series memory cables.  You will typically want the 17-01534-*
  series memory cables, IIRC, for the MS650-series configurations.

