Actually, the PMI cable can make a big difference, even in MVIIs.

We had a MVII that originally came with 9MB.  When we upgraded to 16MB, 
we got random memory parity error crashes.  These were fixed by 
replacing the original PMI cable (bare ribbon cable) with a shielded one.

