I've never used an IDE disk drive on either Prioris or Celebris XL computers,
only SCSI.  If I had to make a wild guess, I would say that the limit would be
either 2.1GB or 8.4GB, most likely the latter.  Beginning with early Pentium
computers, the BIOS was limited to 8.4GB, but DEC could have been a laggard
here, given that most of the machines were SCSI.   All I can suggest is to see
what capacity of IDE drive the BIOS recognizes.  Low capacity IDE drives are
plentiful and cheap.

BTW, the on-board SCSI BIOS limit is only 4.2GB, so people who want to break the
storage capacity limitations of these computers invariably add either a SCSI
host adapter or an IDE controller card... Ben Myers

